---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  Breadcrumb,
  BreadcrumbItem,
  BreadcrumbLink,
  BreadcrumbList,
  BreadcrumbPage,
  BreadcrumbSeparator,
} from '@/components/ui/breadcrumb';
import { Separator } from '@/components/ui/separator';
import { t } from '../i18n/load';
import { personSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const site = Astro.site?.toString().replace(/\/$/u, '') ?? 'https://awaketab.com';
const crumbLink = 'inline-flex min-h-11 items-center';
const inlineLink = 'text-primary underline underline-offset-4';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={t('page.about.title')}
  description={t('page.about.description')}
  canonical={`${site}/about`}
  ogImage="/og/about-en.png"
  schema={personSchema()}
>
  <header class="at-page-header"><a class="at-wordmark" href="/">AwakeTab</a></header>
  <main class="mx-auto mt-6 w-full max-w-[45rem] leading-relaxed">
    <Breadcrumb aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <BreadcrumbList>
        <BreadcrumbItem>
          <BreadcrumbLink className={crumbLink} href="/">{t('app.name')}</BreadcrumbLink>
        </BreadcrumbItem>
        <BreadcrumbSeparator />
        <BreadcrumbItem>
          <BreadcrumbPage>{t('page.about.h1')}</BreadcrumbPage>
        </BreadcrumbItem>
      </BreadcrumbList>
    </Breadcrumb>
    <section class="mt-4 space-y-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight">{t('page.about.h1')}</h1>
      <p>
        AwakeTab is an independent project built and maintained by Soubhik Biswas. Its purpose is narrow:
        request a browser wake lock, show the result honestly, and make the common timer and until-time
        workflows fast without requiring an account.
      </p>
    </section>
    <Separator className="my-8" />
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How it is tested</h2>
      <p>
        The lock layer is tested as a seven-state transition machine. Browser journeys inject a controllable
        Wake Lock implementation and verify acquisition, denial, release on hidden tabs, reacquisition,
        fallback behavior and multi-tab warnings. Device claims are kept in the support matrix and are
        refreshed separately from application code.
      </p>
    </section>
    <Separator className="my-8" />
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What AwakeTab will not claim</h2>
      <p>
        A normal browser tab cannot guarantee operation while hidden, prevent system sleep after a laptop
        lid closes, or override battery-saving policy. AwakeTab does not simulate mouse movement or
        keystrokes and does not claim to keep chat presence indicators available.
      </p>
      <p>
        The awake screen carries no advertising or third-party scripts. The core wake-lock package is
        developed as open-source software so its state transitions can be inspected independently.
      </p>
      <p>
        If AwakeTab is useful, you can <a class={inlineLink} href="https://buymeacoffee.com/awaketab" rel="noopener" target="_blank">buy Soubhik a coffee</a>.
        There is no widget, account, or extra script — just a link.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
